    {
      "id": "MHC-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-maximal-unimodular-extension",
      "title": "A marked unimodular extension absorbs the defect",
      "hypotheses": "An inert bad place for a maximal lattice and a common fixed-field uniformizer π. A local orthogonal basis has exactly one entry a of valuation one.",
      "statement": "L=M+R(cx+e)/π is self-dual for h⊥⟨π⟩ when c has norm congruent to −π/a. It contains e with a pairing witness of value one and intersects the original space in M.",
